Build software with a verifiable network ledger

Usage:
  warden [command]

Available Commands:
  build       Run a build with network auditing
  clean       Remove orphaned warden containers, networks, and images
  completion  Generate the autocompletion script for the specified shell
  doctor      Preflight the host for the selected driver
  help        Help about any command
  hyperv      Hyper-V privileged helper service (Windows host)
  image       Prepare and list build-guest base images (VM drivers)
  inspect     Verify and display a build ledger
  setup       Prepare the host for the selected driver (one time, idempotent)
  shell       Open an interactive shell in the build environment

Flags:
      --color string     color output (auto, always, never)
      --config string    config file to read, the only one that is (default: WARDEN_CONFIG, then ./warden.toml if it exists)
      --driver string    orchestration driver (container, qemu, vz, hyperv, firecracker)
  -h, --help             help for warden
      --runtime string   container runtime (finch, docker, podman)
  -v, --verbose          verbose output
      --version          version for warden

Use "warden [command] --help" for more information about a command.
